|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">[[Lumpy Space People|Lumpy]] Jake</h3>
|[[File: Lumpy Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Trouble in Lumpy Space]]," Jake was turned lumpy during the [[Mallow Tea Ceremony]] when [[Lumpy Space Princess]] falls on him and bites him causing Jake to get [[The lumps]]. When he turned back to normal Jake, he was at [[Promcoming]] and he fell on the antidote that Finn brought. He is pink and his face looks the same. He only has four lumps, not including his tail and talks like Lumpy Space Princess. He also developed an attitude similar to Lumpy Space Princess. Lumpy Jake is hated by Lumpy Finn.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Jake's subconscious</h3>
|[[File:JakesSubconscious.png|thumb|center]]
|Jake's subconscious is the subconscious manifestation of Jake that appears in the episode "[[The Witch's Garden]]." He is first seen at the [[River of Junk]] when Jake said that crossing the river looked hard. Jake's subconscious then appears before Jake and also tells him that it is too hard to cross the river and that Jake should simply wear a hat instead. This suggests that Jake's subconscious has a personality similar to Jake's. He later appears when Jake is making his appeal to the [[Witch]] in order to get his powers back. When Jake refuses to give in to the Witch's humiliating demands, Jake's subconscious tells Jake that he is the subconscious form of Jake's old magical self, and is, therefore, beginning to die. This makes Jake start to cry and apologize. The Witch is thoroughly happy with Jake's sorrow and decides to take pity on him. She returns his powers and subsequently restores the vitality of his subconscious self. Jake and his subconscious then leave the Witch's garden in laughter after Jake takes away the Witch's cane, rendering her powerless.

Although Jake's subconscious is translucent and merely Jake's subconscious, he is still solid as when Jake cried over his dying body, tears ran off to his sides. This also means that Jake's subconscious can affect the material plane, as shown when he passes the hat to Jake; he also blames his subconscious for somehow getting a donut, so it could've been that his subconscious actually went and brought it to Jake. It can be assumed that only magical beings can see Jake's subconscious because while Jake was having a vibrant conversation with his subconscious, Finn tells him to "stop talking to yourself!" (however, since Jake's subconscious is himself, Jake, another interpretation could be that Finn literally meant that Jake should stop talking to "himself.") The Witch who stripped Jake of his magical powers was also somehow able to see him and hear him.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Groucho</h3>
|[[File: Groucho Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|When entering the [[Spiky Village]] in the episode "[[Gut Grinder (episode)|Gut Grinder]]"; Finn gave Jake a pair of "Groucho glasses" so that the Spiky People would not think Jake was the Gut Grinder. Jake donned the combination glasses/nose/mustache and introduced himself as "Groucho," a clear homage to {{w|Groucho Marx}}. He walks on four legs, sports a much wider body (to the proportion of a horse, or a similarly-sized animal) and wears the glasses on a fake head, while his face lies hidden between the front two legs.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Gut Grinder</h3>
|[[File: Gut Grinder Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|Even though Jake was not the [[Sharon#The Gut Grinder|Gut Grinder]], he believed himself to be the Gut Grinder so much he became one. [[Soft People]], [[Cube People]], and [[Spiky People]] all thought that Jake was the Gut Grinder. Once he believes he is the gut grinder, his eyes become black and white spirals (most likely to emphasize his craziness). And throughout the episode, the scared townspeople thought Jake was the Gut Grinder. The Gut Grinder was actually [[Sharon]] the [[Spiky Mayor|mayor]]'s wife, who made her costume look like Jake because she thought he was hot. The actual gut grinder costume looks similar to Jake, but with dark orange, rough fur, and the same crazy spiral eyes (he also carries a mace which looks like Jake's face, with pink spikes and a white and pink striped handle).
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Rainicorn Jake</h3>
|[[File:Ritchie Blackmore's R~A~I~N~B~O~W.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode, "Her Parents," Jake dresses up like a Rainicorn to impress Lady's parents. In his imagination, he has stripes in light pink, dark pink, purple, neon green, yellow, and salmon (the legs have the same pattern as Lady's legs). In reality, he is simply covered in ketchup and mustard.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Jakesuit</h3>
|[[File:S5e27_Jakesuit.png|thumb|center]]
|The Jakesuit first appears in "[[The Silent King]]." This is the only way the [[goblins]] will not see their "[[Finn|King]]" being 'un-kingly.' The Jakesuit consists of Jake as armor with a hole for Finn's face; the hole looks like the hole on [[Finn's hat]]. This suit makes it's user look extra muscular, although that's just because of Jake's stretchy powers.

The Jakesuit returns again in the episodes "[[Jake Suit]]", "[[Reboot]],"  and "Together Again".
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Conductor</h3>
|[[File:Candy_Conductor.png|thumb|center]]
|The Conductor is the main antagonist in "[[Mystery Train]]." He is seen with a winking, smiling, and blushing (all at once), and his pink head is much wider than his body. He wears a blue suit and hat. Throughout the episode, he comes and goes during the train ride, and begins creeping [[Finn]] out. Not until all other suspects are dead is he actually suspected of murdering all the candy people, because according to Finn, "It's never the creepy guy who's the murderer." After supposedly "''murdering''" everybody, including Jake, an enraged Finn chases him across the entire length of the train. After a short one-on-one battle in the train's control room, he is revealed to be Jake in disguise-via pink and blue paint and his stretchy powers. The paint may be some sort of liquid candy since Jake licked it off of himself after he revealed himself.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Magic Fist</h3>
|[[File:Magic_Fist.png|thumb|center]]
|Magic Fist is the disguise Finn and Jake wore in "[[Wizard Battle]]" in order to be eligible to compete. Finn and Jake wear a big red trench coat, a blue hood, and dark blue shades. Only Finn's face and Jake's arms and legs can be seen, and the rest is kept under the coat. Jake was the 'magic second head' of Magic Fist and Magic Fist's Limbs are Jake's arms and legs. Since Jake cannot see while his head is inside the cloak, Finn tells Jake where to attack with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clock_position| clock position code].
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Randy Butternubs</h3>
|[[File: Randy Butternubs.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[The Creeps]]," Jake wears a tall top hat with a green mask along with a purple cape with a tuxedo and a bow tie. He also wears black shoes. Jake shows a lack of appreciation for his alias when he throws the card on the ground.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">[[Zombies|Zombie]] Jake</h3>
|[[File:Zombie Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|Zombie Jake appears in "[[From Bad to Worse]]," when he was bitten by [[Mr. Candy Cane]] as a [[Candy People|Candy Zombie]]. Zombie Jake looks like Jake, but with dark yellow-gray skin and cracks throughout his skin, along with dark-rimmed light green eyes. Zombie Jake is the first zombie to be cured in "From Bad to Worse," but turns back into a zombie merely seconds later after being bitten again. A different version of Zombie Jake appears in the Adventure Time game, [[Rhythm Heroes]].
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Baron of the Grasslands</h3>
|[[File: Baron of the Grasslands.png|thumb|center]]
|In "Incendium," Jake claims to be the "Baron of the Grasslands," and an envoy of "Prince" Finn. Jake pretended that he was of royal blood to court [[Flame Princess]] for Finn, but later on, discovers that Flame Princess is evil. He is seen blue because he is using [[Flame Powers#Flame Shield|flame shield]]; this also causes his backpack and boots to look blue. He is seen using a flame guitar while in this persona, which he uses to sing "[[All Warmed Up Inside]]".
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Demon Jake</h3>
|[[File:Demon Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|Demon Jake appears in "[[Daddy's Little Monster]]" so they can sneak into the Nightosphere. He sings "[[Political Rap]]" in this form. Jake looks like a quadrupedal demon with big and sharp teeth. He has pointy ears, his eyes are black with white diamonds in the center, and an extra large jaw to showcase the many pointy teeth.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Milkman/Mailman Jake</h3>
|[[File:Milkman and Mailman Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Princess Cookie (episode)|Princess Cookie]]," Jake dresses as a milkman in order to try to rescue the hostages (he wanted to dress as a milkman, but [[Princess Bubblegum]] said it wasn't realistic). Finn dresses in an outfit similar to that of a ninja, pretending to be Jake's shadow. At the end of the episode, dressed as a mailman, he delivers a daisy crown to [[Princess Cookie (character)|Baby-Snaps]]. His milkman outfit is a simple white suit and cap, with a black tie, belt, and boots. His mailman outfit is a white button-up t-shirt with blue shorts held up by the same belt, a tan safari hat, and a blue satchel filled with mail.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Female Cinnamon Bun</h3>
|[[File:FCFCBF24-4FF7-423D-9244-6E1B80717FE8.jpeg|thumb|center]]
|In the episode, "[[All Your Fault]]," Jake is shapeshifted to look like a female [[Cinnamon Bun]]. He also wears a pink bow and is called "girlfriend" by Cinnamon Bun. This is not the same as the [[Cinnamon Bun in Dress|Cinnamon Bun gender-swap]]; although both have bows on their head, Jake's is pink, while the gender-swap's is green (she also has a green dress, while Jake's version has no clothes).
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Finn's memory Jake</h3>
|[[File:Puhoy Finn's memory of Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|{{main|Imaginary Jake}}
In the episode "[[Puhoy]]," Elder Finn has a flashback about Jake, but he looks odd and morphed. His nose and jowls are further up, in between his eyes. His jowls also appear to be longer than usual. His eyes are the opposite color, with the outsides white and the insides black. Also, he has three white hairs on his head. He also gives different advice than actual Jake did.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">[[Pete Sassafras]]'s lawyer</h3>
|[[File:S5 e25 Pete and his fake lawyer.PNG|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Candy Streets]]" when Pete Sassafras is in the [[Candy Dungeon]], Finn and Jake are interrogating Pete. Because they are certain he is guilty, as a joke, Jake makes a fake lawyer sprout from himself. The lawyer lets Pete know that he is ultimately guilty, and Pete is obviously a little confused by this. He looks to have short hair, wide eyes, and a shirt and tie (although this is made completely of Jake's skin).
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">JMO</h3>
|[[File:S5e28_JMO.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Be More]]," Jake shapeshifts into a [[MOs|MO]] in order to gain entrance to the [[MO Co.]] There is no known JMO created by [[Moe]], although it can be assumed that there is one for every letter, and that we simply haven't seen a real JMO before.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Blue Nose</h3>
|[[File:B11891BE-BF0B-472C-9E1C-D88ADACD5133.jpeg|thumb|center]]
|{{main|Blue Nose}}
Blue Nose is the main character in the episode, "[[Sad Face]]." He's Jake's tail wearing a small black fedora, and makeup to depict a white face, red frown, and blue nose. He takes on a mind of his own and joins the [[Traveling Mini Circus]] in order to free [[Goralina]] from the grasp of the [[Ringmaster]]. In the end, he was successful.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Sheet Ghost Jake</h3>
|[[File: 4A00723C-27CF-4870-93EF-8BB99EF7606B.jpeg|thumb|center]]
|In the episode, "[[Ghost Fly]]", in an attempt to stop the [[Ghost Fly (character)|Ghost Fly]], Jake gathered some "unfinished business" and was then zapped by [[BMO]] so that he may become a [[Sheet Ghosts|Sheet Ghost]]. In this form, he could enter the same realm as the Ghost Fly and make physical contact with him.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">[[Hermit Eyes]] Forms</h3>
|[[File:Big Brother Jake.png|thumb|center]]
[[File:Wise Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Don't Look]]", Finn acquired a pair of magical eyes that caused people to turn into exactly what he saw them as. When Finn saw Jake as a good older brother, he caused Jake to appear to look like a humanoid with a varsity jacket. He later made Jake into a large eared, wrinkly old man with a cane after Jake shared wise words of advise.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Ice Jake</h3>
|[[File:Jake the Dog Ice Elemental.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Winter Light]]", shortly after entering the [[Ice Elementals|Ice Elemental]] section of Ooo, Jake began to speak depressing remarks as he grew an ice spike on his head. Shortly after this, the rest of his body turned to ice as he held his knees and continued to wallow in sadness. Although [[Patience St. Pim]] said that Jake would never leave, now having succumbed to her element, Finn took Jake anyway. After returning to the [[Cloud Kingdom]], Jake returned to normal.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Slime Jake</h3>
|[[File:Jake the Dog Slime Elemental.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Slime Central]]", Finn and Jake at first disguised themselves as Slime Elementals. However, after going into [[Slime Princess]]' body to retrieve the jewel from her crown, Jake became too comfortable and succumbed to his slime elemental transformation. This caused him to assimilate with Slime Princess until the end of the Elementals series.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">Soul Jake</h3>
|[[File:Soul Jake .png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Together Again]]", when communicating with [[Peppermint Butler]], Finn and Jake appeared to look like blue transparent spirits.
|-
|<h3 style="font-size:1em;">[[Fish]]/[[Mermaids|Mermaid]] Jake</h3>
|[[File:Fish Jake.png|thumb|center]]
[[File:Mermaid Jake.png|thumb|center]]
|In the episode "[[Together Again]]", Finn and Jake possess fish in [[Life]]'s universe, causing them to turn into mermaids. At first, Jake appeared to look more like a normal fish, but was able to change his form to look more like a mermaid.
|}


